<title>JAPAN: Kumagai Gumi, others to expand Singapore subway.</title>
<headline>Kumagai Gumi, others to expand Singapore subway.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kumagai Gumi Co Ltd said on Thursday that a joint venture between it and two other firms had won an 18 billion yen order for subway construction from the Land Transport Authority of Singapore.</p>
<p>Kumagai Gumi, Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd and local contractor Sembawang Engineering and Construction Pte Ltd won an order to build two subway stations and a 2.5-kilometre extension of an existing subway line, Kumagai Gumi said in a statement.</p>
<p>Kumagai and Sembawang Engineering each own 45 percent of the joint venture, with Mitsui holding the rest, the statement said.</p>
<p>Construction will start in June 1998 and will be completed in April 2002, it said.</p>
</text>
